event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_06f339645f964ef1006a82b2d52e708195a11d10edc1deea9e","output_index":0,"sequence_number":83,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Finding the trick in the question**\n\nI'm thinking through the riddle where it says \"all but 9 run away,\" which leads me to realize that 9 must remain. It’s interesting how often riddles twist language to make you think differently. So, if all but 9 are gone, then those 9 are the ones that stay behind. I’m curious how this kind of wording plays with expectations—it’s a fun puzzle to solve!"}

